{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness","id":808613,"title":"[2ed] Changeling weakeness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-14T06:13:39-08:00","id":808613,"title":"[2ed] Changeling weakeness","content":"Does somebody know about the new rules for cold iron and another weakness about changelings?<br /> <br /> In the doc about the Hunt\u200bsmen seems like they suffer aggravated damage from iron and arcadian weapons.<br /> Changelings now suffer aggravated damage from iron too?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T06:29:28-08:00","id":808622,"title":"","content":"I don't think the specifics of how iron affects Changelings have been spoiled yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T06:35:49-08:00","id":808627,"title":"","content":"A part of me hopes iron becomes a more potent bane to the Lost besides being able to bypass their magics. Maybe not outright aggravated damage, perhaps. Additional damage, maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T08:36:42-08:00","id":808731,"title":"","content":"One thing I do know is that the &quot;cold&quot; has been dropped. If people tend to think of it as iron, it's iron as far as weaknesses are concerned. (That's why steel doesn't work, even though it's more iron than iron).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T08:44:47-08:00","id":808735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=808731#post808731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I do know is that the &amp;quot;cold&amp;quot; has been dropped. If people tend to think of it as iron, it's iron as far as weaknesses are concerned. (That's why steel doesn't work, even though it's more iron than iron).</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind, however, that the Elemental Seeming Curse, which has been previewed, says that it causes them to suffer a Condition related to their element when struck by cold iron. So we can safely assume that cold iron must still be a thing, even if its definition is changing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T08:47:46-08:00","id":808738,"title":"","content":"Unless that was written before the change was made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T09:13:40-08:00","id":808758,"title":"","content":"Fair point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T09:59:36-08:00","id":808790,"title":"","content":"This is what I'll be using for my game when <i>Changeling:The Lost 2e</i> comes out:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Homebrew of Pale_Crusader</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>(Switch-able) Cold Wrought Iron</b><br /> Injuries inflicted by Cold Wrought Iron are cannot be regenerated or healed via supernatural means, it counts as resistant damage of the type normally associated with the damage inflicted. Supernaturally provided armors and supernatural powers don't provide protection from weapons made of Cold Wrought Iron. While exposed to Cold Wrought Iron the supernatural being's max die pool for any action is capped by their Morality Advantage. In addition when directly in contact with Cold Wrought Iron to the supernatural takes 1 point of Aggravated damage per Permanent Atrocity they have per combat turn. Supernatural powers used by a being with this bane do not work while in contact with Cold Wrought Iron. Abilities of a supernatural to rise from the dead do not work if this bane was involved with their death.<br /> <br /> <b>===Side Bar===<br /> ====Balancing banes====</b><br /> <i>Note for clarity: &quot;Cold&quot; is an additional quality of the wrought iron, not a production technique, ei the wrought iron must be cold for the bane to apply. This additional requirement is due to wrought iron being much more common than silver that more specific requirements are justified when choosing it as a bane, consider it metaphysical loopholes that balance the cosmic scales of justice. Sunlight is extremely common but its availability is not under direct control of the wielder. When the storyteller is arbitrating the balance new Personal Banes against existing banes they should consider these factors and teak the specific to towards balance with their best judgement. The listed examples are the benchmarks for this process.</i><br /> ========<br /> =======</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize that it references a bunch of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\">my homebrew rules</a>, but I thought it would still be useful for this discussion. As a side note I've already included Huntsmen into my homebrew mechanics. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-14-2016, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:02:29-08:00","id":808794,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna go out on a limb, with all the talking we've done, and answer this.<br /> <br /> So, iron, that which is perceived to be iron(by who, I have to ask), cuts through fae magic. Contracts, Tokens, Hedgespun Artifacts, the like-Iron cuts through it.<br /> <br /> Cold Iron is defined as iron that has been shaped by hand-no machines beyond simple ones, no magic to shape or transform it. Cold Iron does aggravated damage to fairys. Strangers, Huntsmen, Hobgoblins, <i>and Changelings</i>, they all burn under cold iron's caress. Should a fairy touch cold iron, they subtract their Wyrd from all dice pools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T03:48:10-08:00","id":809483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=808794#post808794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cold Iron is defined as iron that has been shaped by hand-no machines beyond simple ones, no magic to shape or transform it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have one question to this - Would using honing Skills by magic, not the magic on the weapon itself, would make Iron not Cold? In other words - can I have magical blacksmith ( like Wizened, some Entaitlment or Forge Master mage ) could use magic on himself to produce better or quicker Cold Iron weapons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-15-2016, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T08:16:12-08:00","id":809592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=808794#post808794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna go out on a limb, with all the talking we've done, and answer this.<br /> So, iron, that which is perceived to be iron(by who, I have to ask), cuts through fae magic. Contracts, Tokens, Hedgespun Artifacts, the like-Iron cuts through it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So anything made from iron? (So steel, right? If not, why not? It's not like it has less iron than something like wrought iron. And no, no one's ever actually used pure iron in any form for anything. The purest irons are high-carbon steel.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=808794#post808794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cold Iron is defined as iron that has been shaped by hand-no machines beyond simple ones, no magic to shape or transform it. Cold Iron does aggravated damage to fairys. Strangers, Huntsmen, Hobgoblins, <i>and Changelings</i>, they all burn under cold iron's caress. Should a fairy touch cold iron, they subtract their Wyrd from all dice pools.</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically hand-made high-carbon steel. That's actually pretty rarified in this day and age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T09:04:45-08:00","id":809627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809483#post809483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have one question to this - Would using honing Skills by magic, not the magic on the weapon itself, would make Iron not Cold? In other words - can I have magical blacksmith ( like Wizened, some Entaitlment or Forge Master mage ) could use magic on himself to produce better or quicker Cold Iron weapons?</div> </div> </div> </div> I would like to know the answer to this as well. In addition, is it forbidden to use magic to make a meteorite fall on Earth so its iron can be turned into weapons (or better yet, aimed directly at a True Fae's face)? I have read that fae magic cannot conjure cold iron, nor transmute something into it. However, could a Mage who is versed in the Matter and/or Prime Arcana conjure true cold iron? I generally assume for the sake of preserving conflict that conjured matter only mimics the mundane properties, not the mystical ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T09:25:44-08:00","id":809643,"title":"","content":"Arisen vs. True Fae. Inexorable Fate vs. Willful Mutable Fate. Ready? FIGHT!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T09:28:55-08:00","id":809646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809592#post809592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So anything made from iron? (So steel, right? If not, why not? It's not like it has less iron than something like wrought iron. And no, no one's ever actually used pure iron in any form for anything. The purest irons are high-carbon steel.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So basically hand-made high-carbon steel. That's actually pretty rarified in this day and age.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, Is steel perceived as iron? It's not at my table, but it might be at yours.<br /> <br /> I like the perception aspect being the judging facotrs, but in certain ways it's also very troublesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T09:32:14-08:00","id":809649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809627#post809627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would like to know the answer to this as well. In addition, is it forbidden to use magic to make a meteorite fall on Earth so its iron can be turned into weapons (or better yet, aimed directly at a True Fae's face)? I have read that fae magic cannot conjure cold iron, nor transmute something into it. However, could a Mage who is versed in the Matter and/or Prime Arcana conjure true cold iron? I generally assume for the sake of preserving conflict that conjured matter only mimics the mundane properties, not the mystical ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Answering the mage part.<br /> <br /> No. If it was summoned by magic, any magic, doesn't count. it's just plain ol' iron.<br /> <br /> Dunno about that meteorite thing. Maybe? So long as the magic didn't create it? I dunno. Stuff for supplements.<br /> <br /> Cold Iron is always going to be a pain in the ass, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T09:33:54-08:00","id":809650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809483#post809483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have one question to this - Would using honing Skills by magic, not the magic on the weapon itself, would make Iron not Cold? In other words - can I have magical blacksmith ( like Wizened, some Entaitlment or Forge Master mage ) could use magic on himself to produce better or quicker Cold Iron weapons?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't rightly know, though I would wager that so long as you are not shaping/creating the metal itself, you should be fine. Still, that's a penny in the air thing, possibly to be decided at your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T09:54:50-08:00","id":809664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809646#post809646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, Is steel perceived as iron? It's not at my table, but it might be at yours.<br /> <br /> I like the perception aspect being the judging facotrs, but in certain ways it's also very troublesome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, steel is what happens when you heat up iron and pound on it with a hammer. Iron age weapons are steel weapons. The quality may vary but the consistency is pretty much the same XX% iron. No one has ever made anything from pure iron because it's impossible to get all the impurities out. Now you can make some things out of wrought iron but nothing with a sharp edge because wrought iron contains pebbles. There was a discussion of this in the past and honestly only a little research reveals the truth about &quot;iron&quot;. So yeah steel is iron (like 97+% iron). You'd be hard pressed to find anything more iron than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T10:00:13-08:00","id":809669,"title":"","content":"No, I know that. I worked metal for three years.<br /> <br /> I just don't assume everyone else thinks about that, or how they respond to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T10:06:57-08:00","id":809677,"title":"","content":"The way I'll probably rule this is that iron harms the fae because it's humanity's labour. With the True Fae as a thinly-veiled analogy for the upper class that does what it wills to the peasants (since they are, after all, <i>the Gentry</i>), the difference between iron and steel is not of composition, but of use. The ugly, black iron is the metal of the servants, the workers, the filthy underclass. Shiny steel, on the other hand, is a metal fit for a noble's sword.<br /> <br /> And cold iron is such a bane because it represents <i>toil</i>. Fae don't have to truly work for anything; what their magic can't provide, an enslaved servant will. Hammering on a lump of iron until it's sharp, making a crude shank to strike at your master, carries the weight of a million stories with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T10:26:18-08:00","id":809695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809664#post809664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, steel is what happens when you heat up iron and pound on it with a hammer. Iron age weapons are steel weapons. The quality may vary but the consistency is pretty much the same XX% iron. No one has ever made anything from pure iron because it's impossible to get all the impurities out. Now you can make some things out of wrought iron but nothing with a sharp edge because wrought iron contains pebbles. There was a discussion of this in the past and honestly only a little research reveals the truth about &amp;quot;iron&amp;quot;. So yeah steel is iron (like 97+% iron). You'd be hard pressed to find anything more iron than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all true, but has nothing to do with what makes something Iron for the purposes of harming the fae. Nevermind that the stuff we call steel has a higher Fe content than the stuff we call iron, the Fae are creatures of story, and stories care not one wit about the molecular composition of the hero's weapon. They do care if the weapon is a finely-honed, shining blade, forged with the specific intention of piercing human flesh, or if it's a crude lump of dark metal, barely sharp enough to even be used for its purpose as a farming tool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809677#post809677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I'll probably rule this is that iron harms the fae because it's humanity's labour. With the True Fae as a thinly-veiled analogy for the upper class that does what it wills to the peasants (since they are, after all, <i>the Gentry</i>), the difference between iron and steel is not of composition, but of use. The ugly, black iron is the metal of the servants, the workers, the filthy underclass. Shiny steel, on the other hand, is a metal fit for a noble's sword.<br /> <br /> And cold iron is such a bane because it represents <i>toil</i>. Fae don't have to truly work for anything; what their magic can't provide, an enslaved servant will. Hammering on a lump of iron until it's sharp, making a crude shank to strike at your master, carries the weight of a million stories with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really cool take on it. In particular, the part about steel vs. iron being defined by its use I think is a better way to explain it than perception, since perception is so subjective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-15-2016, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T10:40:14-08:00","id":809703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809677#post809677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I'll probably rule this is that iron harms the fae because it's humanity's labour. With the True Fae as a thinly-veiled analogy for the upper class that does what it wills to the peasants (since they are, after all, <i>the Gentry</i>), the difference between iron and steel is not of composition, but of use. The ugly, black iron is the metal of the servants, the workers, the filthy underclass. Shiny steel, on the other hand, is a metal fit for a noble's sword.<br /> <br /> And cold iron is such a bane because it represents <i>toil</i>. Fae don't have to truly work for anything; what their magic can't provide, an enslaved servant will. Hammering on a lump of iron until it's sharp, making a crude shank to strike at your master, carries the weight of a million stories with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You win the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T11:36:40-08:00","id":809745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809695#post809695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a really cool take on it. In particular, the part about steel vs. iron being defined by its use I think is a better way to explain it than perception, since perception is so subjective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! My general rule would be &quot;if you were an amoral aristocrat in the dark ages, would you design this as peasant use or would you consider it using as your own?&quot;. There's a lot of gray area, and that's okay. Maybe you craft an iron sword <i>too well</i> and it becomes worthy steel instead. If you want to make absolutely sure you're using iron, you have to pick the ugliest, least useful weapon available, or deliberately forge it poorly. It will give you penalties to wield it, it has no bonus damage (maybe it has <i>negative</i> bonus damage, since it's so ill-forged), but hey, at least you got what you wanted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809703#post809703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You win the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":10056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","user":"ShadowKnight1224","date":". 01-15-2016, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T11:58:20-08:00","id":809764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809677#post809677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I'll probably rule this is that iron harms the fae because it's humanity's labour. With the True Fae as a thinly-veiled analogy for the upper class that does what it wills to the peasants (since they are, after all, <i>the Gentry</i>), the difference between iron and steel is not of composition, but of use. The ugly, black iron is the metal of the servants, the workers, the filthy underclass. Shiny steel, on the other hand, is a metal fit for a noble's sword.<br /> <br /> And cold iron is such a bane because it represents <i>toil</i>. Fae don't have to truly work for anything; what their magic can't provide, an enslaved servant will. Hammering on a lump of iron until it's sharp, making a crude shank to strike at your master, carries the weight of a million stories with it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809745#post809745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks! My general rule would be &quot;if you were an amoral aristocrat in the dark ages, would you design this as peasant use or would you consider it using as your own?&quot;. There's a lot of gray area, and that's okay. Maybe you craft an iron sword <i>too well</i> and it becomes worthy steel instead. If you want to absolutely sure you're using iron, you have to pick the ugliest, least useful weapon available, or deliberately forge it poorly. It will give you penalties to wield it, it has no bonus damage (maybe it has <i>negative</i> bonus damage, since it's so ill-forged), but hey, at least you got what you wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div> <i>Brilliant.</i> I can vividly imagine a hard-working Summer courtier using this idea as the basis for a badass speech to an especially lazy and entitled True Fae after the changeling uses these flaws to trap the monster, and then they hack it to bits with cold iron.<br /> <br /> &quot;Enough is <b>enough</b>! I've HAD IT with these motherfucking Gentry in this motherfucking Freehold!&quot;<br /> <br /> But, you know, more eloquent. I no write gud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 01-15-2016, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T13:04:29-08:00","id":809811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809764#post809764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Brilliant.</i> I can vividly imagine a hard-working Summer courtier using this idea as the basis for a badass speech to an especially lazy and entitled True Fae after the changeling uses these flaws to trap the monster, and then they hack it to bits with cold iron.<br /> <br /> &quot;Enough is <b>enough</b>! I've HAD IT with these motherfucking Gentry in this motherfucking Freehold!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Summer Court: Where laborers are working their (ex)masters to death. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T15:45:37-08:00","id":809882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809669#post809669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I know that. I worked metal for three years.<br /> <br /> I just don't assume everyone else thinks about that, or how they respond to that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Anyone who's read the Dresden Files thinks of steel as iron when it comes to the Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T17:06:07-08:00","id":809935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809882#post809882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Anyone who's read the Dresden Files thinks of steel as iron when it comes to the Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not everyone's read the Dresden Files.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T17:55:04-08:00","id":809961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809935#post809935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not everyone's read the Dresden Files.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know, but the numerous books are NY Times best sellers, represent a significant fanbase for modern urban fantasy / horror, include a significant fae component, and share many fans with the CofD. It was also only meant as one example of steel = iron among others.<br /> <br /> Additionally, since steel is actually iron, a great many regular people do indeed <i>perceive</i> steel as iron. As steel is fairly ubiquitous, particularly in melee weaponry, what actually constitutes &quot;iron&quot; in Changeling 2e is fairly important. Using just &quot;perception&quot; as the standard, without more detail or greater clarification, might just replace the old &quot;cold iron&quot; debates with something new, rather than eliminating the issue entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T18:51:53-08:00","id":809999,"title":"","content":"I think the big issue of all the cold iron debates is that they are all far too focused on &quot;what&quot;. As noted up thread, just about all forms of useful iron are technically &quot;steel&quot; , and trying to figure out what makes it cold iron has been contentious to say the least.<br /> <br /> I have latched on the Shadowknights idea that the &quot;how&quot; - the process by which the item was crafted, carries more weight. You can have two blades, one a well made but mass-produced item with optimum iron to carbon ratio and forged with the most modern tools available, the other a blade recently made, but using old techniques - working by hand and simple tool from ore to finished product. The mass-produced item wouldn't even tickle one of the Gentry, while the hand-made weapon could cut him down in a blow.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the iron is a symbol, and the forging is a story. And only a Story can kill a Story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 01-15-2016, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T20:00:47-08:00","id":810034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809961#post809961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, since steel is actually iron, a great many regular people do indeed <i>perceive</i> steel as iron. As steel is fairly ubiquitous, particularly in melee weaponry, what actually constitutes &quot;iron&quot; in Changeling 2e is fairly important. Using just &quot;perception&quot; as the standard, without more detail or greater clarification, might just replace the old &quot;cold iron&quot; debates with something new, rather than eliminating the issue entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just think the <b>ShadowKnight</b>'s explanation <b><i>should</i></b> be included in <b>Changeling</b> 2ED corebook under appropriate section - it's much more coherent than &quot;perception&quot;, totally correct from gameline standpoint ( or at least how I see it from reading half of 1ED books ) and is simple. Steel is for nobility, Iron is for &quot;peasants&quot;, by the rules of Ancient Contract - and this why it's anathema to the <i>Gentry. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T20:25:41-08:00","id":810046,"title":"","content":"It's definitely something I would include into the story of how the Fae broke the contract with Iron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T20:52:48-08:00","id":810059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=809961#post809961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I know, but the numerous books are NY Times best sellers, represent a significant fanbase for modern urban fantasy / horror, include a significant fae component, and share many fans with the CofD. It was also only meant as one example of steel = iron among others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also were based on the author's Mage chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T21:13:20-08:00","id":810067,"title":"","content":"I've also always been very partial to the story of iron as mankind's defence. The iron fence around the graveyard, the iron gate at the castle, the iron spikes on the stone walls.<br /> <br /> Maybe once the True Fae betrayed iron, iron decided to become mankind's best friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T23:04:19-08:00","id":810100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=810059#post810059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also were based on the author's Mage chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Really? I read that Butcher's fiction was inspired by the Anita Blake series and he was a tabletop role-player, but I never heard that he based anything in the DF on his rpg experiences, no less Mage (classic or CofD).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T20:05:11-08:00","id":811493,"title":"","content":"There was a young adult novel called 'The Secret Hour' by Scott Westerfeld, that I thought had an interesting take on the vulnerability to cold iron. In it, there were creatures that very fae like creatures called Darklings who hunted mankind for sport. They couldn't be harmed by anything that they recognized, so the only way to hurt them was with something new. The stories about them being hurt by &quot;cold iron&quot; were from the early days of the iron age, when being able to forge iron had only just been discovered and so it still hurt them. In the present their weakness was to new exotic alloys, so hunters would usually make their weapons out of hubcaps bought from specialty car dealerships.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T21:09:39-08:00","id":811527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/808613-2ed-changeling-weakeness?p=811493#post811493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a young adult novel called 'The Secret Hour' by Scott Westerfeld, that I thought had an interesting take on the vulnerability to cold iron. In it, there were creatures that very fae like creatures called Darklings who hunted mankind for sport. They couldn't be harmed by anything that they recognized, so the only way to hurt them was with something new. The stories about them being hurt by &amp;quot;cold iron&amp;quot; were from the early days of the iron age, when being able to forge iron had only just been discovered and so it still hurt them. In the present their weakness was to new exotic alloys, so hunters would usually make their weapons out of hubcaps bought from specialty car dealerships.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> They were also vulnerable to the number 13, and that was the first of a trilogy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}